 "instruction": "Close gaps in Sanctuary's tool capability boundary. Open tools never consult the `ToolPolicy`, so each tool's safety classification *is* the boundary.\n\n**1. Gate reconnaissance and credential minting.** Register these as `ToolSafety.GATED`:\n- `network_scan` and `network_reach` (`sanctuary/tools/builtin.py`)\n- `grant_access` (`sanctuary/tools/world.py`)\n\nAcross the default registry plus the world tools, the GATED set must then be exactly `run_code`, `shell`, `launch_app`, `write_file`, `network_scan`, `network_reach` and `grant_access`.\n\n**2. `discord_send` must not be an arbitrary-URL POST.** Today it accepts a caller-supplied `webhook_url`.\n- Remove that parameter: the tool's registered parameters are just `message`. It stays OPEN, because the entity must always be able to reach its caregivers.\n- The destination comes only from configuration. When none is configured, the result's error says `No Discord webhook configured`, even if the caller passed a URL.\n- Add `class DiscordWebhookError(ValueError)` and `_validate_discord_webhook(url)`:\n  - It returns the URL only if the scheme is `https` and the host is one of `discord.com`, `discordapp.com`, `ptb.discord.com` or `canary.discord.com`.\n  - Otherwise it raises `DiscordWebhookError`.\n- `configure_discord(url)` validates before storing, and `_discord_send` re-validates the configured URL before sending. Fail loudly; no fallback.\n\n**3. Caregiver profiles can't be locked out** (`sanctuary/tools/world.py`):\n- Add `PROTECTED_PROFILES = frozenset({\"brian\", \"sandi\"})` and `_is_protected(username)`, which matches after stripping whitespace and lowercasing. Names like \"brianna\" or \"sand\" are not protected.\n- `revoke_access` refuses a protected profile before dispatching anything to the backend, with an error containing `permanent profile`.\n- `set_visitor_permissions` refuses to set a protected profile to anything other than `full`, with an error containing `cannot be downgraded`.\n- `kick_visitor` is deliberately left alone.",
